s for teenagers with autism as  in any aspect of autism treatment or  trying to learn about autism the  treatment really needs to vary by the  characteristics of the person there are  a number of things going on right here  at Yale Dennis Sadowski is involved in  cognitive behavioral therapies for  anxiety  irritability and teenagers with autism  Pamela ventola and expert in pivotal  response therapy is developing  applications of that kind of treatment  for teenagers as well psychoanalysis and  autism has a complicated history in the  1950s  and psycho psycho analysis was a very  common approach to understanding  behavior there was a idea that autism  was caused by parenting styles and we  know that that's not true the other  autism is based in jeans and based on  biology  the reasons a person chooses to behave  in a certain way are very very  complicated to understand from a person  who isn't the person behaving and that's  true for a person with autism and it's  true for people without autism many  times people with autism can act in ways  that are considered rude by other people  but it's unintentional one of the  difficulties that many foo dog doesn't  have is understanding the feelings the  thoughts the ideas of other people and  put being able to put themselves in  another person's shoes so your question  makes me wonder if this person that  you're having difficulty with might  benefit from a conversation with you  helping him understand how their actions  are affecting your feelings whether  oxygen can be cured or not is a very  controversial question with a behavioral  diagnosis like autism you either show  the behaviors and make diagnosis or you  don't and so if you gave very effective  intervention to a person with autism or  if they learned a great deal they may no  longer show these kinds of behaviors and  they wouldn't qualify for a diagnosis  what's tricky is that they  the same genes and the same brain  structure that they had when they were  showing